{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>Shimon and Levi are brothers.</b> Of one counsel regarding Shechem and regarding Joseph — ״they said each man to his brother, and now come let us kill him״ — who are they? If you say Reuben or Judah — they did not agree to his killing. If you say the sons of the maidservants — their hatred was not whole, as it says ״he was a lad with the sons of Bilhah and with the sons of Zilpah, etc.״; Issachar and Zilpun would not speak before their brothers who were older than them. Perforce, Shimon and Levi are the ones whom their father called 'brothers.'" "<b>Weapons of violence.</b> This craft of murder — חָמָס (violence) is in their hands — it is from the blessing of Esau; it is his craft — ״and you took it by violence from us.״" "<b>Their weapons.</b> A term of weaponry — the sword in Greek is מכי\"ר; Tanchuma. Another interpretation: מְכֵרֹתֵיהֶם — in the land of their sojourn they conducted themselves with weapons of violence, like ״מְכֹרֹתַיִךְ וּמֹלְדֹתַיִךְ״ (Ezekiel 16), and this is the Targum of Onkelos."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:04:04.634493123Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}